    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d313">

                <pb facs="0598" n="538" sameAs="frus:frus1868p2/pg538"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Plumb.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 76.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1868-07-15"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >July</hi> 15, 1868.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to inclose to you a copy of a
                    communication received from T. W. Scott, consul at Matainoras, in reference to
                    the seizure of an amount of gold coin by the custom-house authorities at that
                    port, belonging to Dr. W. L. Huchinson. a citizen of the United States.</p>
                <p>You are instructed to make an investigation of this case and report to this
                    department.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edward L. Plumb</hi>, Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
